# f2 = watch. The program of a-guard-is-asked-in-the-turn-where-a-typed-store-may-create-a-field-from-source.ir.
# The switch testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime checks the walk against itself.
# A read of a slot that may be empty skips the lookup on the prototype chain where the state remembers that the guard of the class holds.
# With the switch, the guard is tested again before such a read, and the process crashes where the guard does not hold.
# The injected fault makes the effects entry of PutSlotOrAdd false: the entry says that the operation invalidates no guard.
# So the second version of the loop tests the guard once, in the preheader, and its iteration relies on that.
# The test that is built again must be in the iteration.
# It is neither resolved from the table of known results nor hoisted to the preheader, because both of those rely on the assumption that it audits.
# There are four tests of the name: the first version's own test and the one built again after it, the second version's test in its preheader and the one built again in its iteration.
# If the test were built like any other operation, there would be three: the check in the iteration would then depend on the test in the preheader and would always pass.
# RUN(LEANS): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Operation/PutSlotOrAdd/MemberGuards
# LEANS-COUNT-2: = AreMembersUnchanged conditions=[{layout=L0 key="note"}]
# LEANS-NOT: source=RememberedFact
# RUN(AGAIN): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Operation/PutSlotOrAdd/MemberGuards,CheckWalkAtRunTime
# AGAIN-COUNT-4: = AreMembersUnchanged conditions=[{layout=L0 key="note"}]
# RUN(INTURN): walk f2 mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Operation/PutSlotOrAdd/MemberGuards,CheckWalkAtRunTime
# INTURN: isLoopHead=true
# INTURN: isLoopHead=true
# INTURN: [[again]]: boolean @Boolean = AreMembersUnchanged conditions=[{layout=L0 key="note"}]
# INTURN-NEXT: CheckProof [[again]] checkedType=true {{*}}source=RememberedFact
# INTURN-NEXT: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}} key="note"
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 0 14 20 above tag
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(BOTH): run-in-shell testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckWalkAtRunTime
# BOTH: 0 14 20 above tag
# BOTH-NEXT: exited with 0
